{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>You shall not eat on the blood.</b> It is expounded with many facets in Sanhedrin (63a): a warning not to eat the flesh of consecrated offerings before the throwing of the blood, and a warning against eating from an unconsecrated animal before its life has departed, and many more." "<b>You shall not divine.</b> Such as those who divine with a weasel and with birds — his bread fell from his mouth, a deer crossed his path (Sifra)." "<b>And you shall not observe times.</b> A term of seasons and hours — he says: such-and-such a day is favorable to begin a task, such-and-such an hour is ill-omened for setting out (Sanhedrin 65a)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:15.925433241Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}